    <statement><p>Which is a parametric equation for the curve <m>16 = \left(x-9\right)^{2}+\left(y+5\right)^{2}</m>?</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(9+4\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),4\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-5\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(4\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-5,9+4\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(9+16\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),16\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-5\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(16\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-5,9+16\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><m>(9, -5)</m>.  Using the parametric representation of a circle we get <m>c(t) = \left(9+4\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),4\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-5\right)</m>.


</solution>
